losk (2.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed keys going nowhere when never-focus was active: LOSK had stopped tracking the target window.
  * Focus is restored through xlib on every keypress, about 0.1 ms instead of 20-30 ms.
  * Status area shows the last key sent and its target window.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 04:00:00 +0000

losk (2.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed keys not typing at all: the 2.5.0 click catcher was swallowing clicks.
  * Typing runs off the reliable clicked signal; repeat can no longer break it.
  * Diagnostics written to ~/.local/share/losk/losk.log so the apps menu works.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 03:00:00 +0000

losk (2.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed keys repeating forever after a single click.
  * Removed two wmctrl subprocess calls that ran on every key click.
  * Added a Repeat toggle and a Fade transparency toggle.
  * Startup diagnostics printed to the terminal.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0000

losk (2.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hold a key to repeat it, including Backspace.
  * Big speed fix: LOSK now asks the window manager never to take keyboard focus, so no xdotool call is needed per keypress.
  * Falls back to the old xdotool path if python3-xlib is unavailable.
  * Vocabulary raised to 730 words and 208 word pairs, with bisect lookup.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0000

losk (2.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Faster typing: removed the blocking --sync on focus return.
  * Focus is only handed back when LOSK actually holds it.
  * Window sized like the Windows OSK, wide and short, with a real minimum.
  * Always-on-top no longer re-asserted on a timer, which caused taskbar flashing.
  * Vocabulary roughly doubled to 560 words and 199 word pairs.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0000

losk (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed keys typing into LOSK instead of your app: focus is now returned before injection.
  * No widget in LOSK can take keyboard focus, so a stray key cannot press a button.
  * Added a Hide button and removed skip_taskbar so minimize works.
  * Next-word prediction and a much larger word list.
  * Optional offline voice input via Vosk.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0000

losk (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keys scale with the window using a homogeneous grid.
  * S/M/L size buttons with matching font scaling.
  * Always-on-top re-asserted every 2 seconds, plus a Pinned toggle.
  * Focus returns to the previous app after each keypress.

 -- ZeshMC <zeshmc@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0000

losk (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * LoskV2 rewrite by ZeshMC.
  * Compact desktop-style layout with correct key widths.
  * Real numeric keypad with tall plus and Enter, duplicate plus removed.
  * Latching modifiers and shifted key labels.
  * Offline word suggestions that learn frequently used words.
  * Graceful fallback when uinput is unavailable.
  * Always-on-top and focus return handling.

